"""You can see the description of the task using the code specified in the title on leetcode.
This program has O(2 ** n) complexity by time and O(2 ** n) by space.

This is a well known algorithmic problem: the Gray code. 
If you’re familiar with it, you have a good chance; 
if not, you’ll have to reinvent it from scratch during a 45-minute interview. 
Even if you don’t grasp the underlying logic, it’s sufficient to simply take the XOR of the current number with that same number shifted one bit to the right.
"""

# https://leetcode.com/problems/gray-code/solutions/1254478/gray-code-by-leetcode-308s/
class Solution:
    def grayCode(self, n: int) -> List[int]:
        return [i ^ (i >> 1) for i in range(1 << n)]

